<p>An AI assistant (Claude, for example) can be connected to the site to draft pages, add posts or update settings for you. Theme Settings &gt; <a href="{{ go.miscellaneous }}">Miscellaneous</a> &gt; <strong>MCP Access</strong> decides exactly what it may touch. Nothing is open until you tick it.</p>
{{ shot( 'ai-access', 'MCP Access: what an AI assistant may read and change.' ) }}
<ol class="guide-steps">
	<li><strong>Post Types</strong>: the kinds of content it may list, read, create and edit (Pages, Posts, News...). Anything not listed is invisible to it.</li>
	<li><strong>Options Pages</strong>: the Theme Settings pages it may read and change.</li>
	<li><strong>Allow Media Uploads</strong>: on, it can add pictures to the Media Library; off, it only uses the ones already there.</li>
	<li><strong>Instructions for AI Assistants</strong>: what it should know before writing: who the site is for, the tone, how pages are put together. It reads this first and cannot change it.</li>
	<li>Click <strong>Save changes</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<ul class="guide-list">
	<li><strong>Never reachable</strong>, whatever is ticked: the Licence, Email, Security, Form Destinations and Tracking pages. They hold passwords, keys and codes that run on every page.</li>
	<li><strong>Everything it changes is recorded</strong>: <em>MCP Activity</em>, at the bottom of the tab, lists the last 20 changes, who made them, and the values a settings page had before.</li>
	<li>Connecting an assistant needs an <em>application password</em> from your profile (Users &gt; Profile). Your developer can set it up.</li>
</ul>
